// The branch predictor (Ref docs: the timing model's Branch prediction):
// a 256-entry BTB, direct mapped by the low 8 bits of the bundle's PC and
// tagged with the rest, shared by all threads. An entry predicts its
// target while its 2-bit counter is below 3 (0 strongly taken). Only
// mispredicts train it: a taken one creates an entry at 0 (or lowers the
// counter and sets the target), a not-taken one raises the counter (or
// creates an entry at 3). MISPREDICTS is checked on the timing model.
//
// Calls and returns are predicted by the same BTB (there is no
// return-address predictor). A function called 3 times from one call
// site: the call and the return each mispredict once (the BTB misses),
// then both are predicted. The loop branch: 2. In all 4.

    || + $r1 ($i64) $r0 2 ;                 // 3 passes
loop:
    || $call f ;
    || ? ($i64) $r1 > --1 $goto loop ;
    || $halt ;
f:
    || + $r2 ($i64) $r2 1  $return ;
